                                "id": "0,7,0,0",
                                "type": 4,
                                "level": 1,
                                "elements": "The condition x>0 is true, so the first branch is executed and the value of the expression becomes x. If x is changed to a negative number, the condition becomes false and the second branch is executed — the expression returns -x. This is an example of calculating the absolute value of a number.",
